---
import '../styles/cage.css';
import GoogleAnalytics from '../components/GoogleAnalytics.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <GoogleAnalytics />
  <title>Site analytics and privacy · Claude Cage</title>
  <link rel="canonical" href={new URL(`${base}privacy/`, Astro.site)} />
  <link rel="icon" href={`${base}cage-icon.png`} />
</head>
<body>
  <main class="wrap privacy-page">
    <a class="text-link" href={base}>← Claude Cage</a>
    <h1>Site analytics and privacy</h1>
    <p>The website and documentation use Google Analytics 4 to count active users, page views, traffic sources and basic visit information such as device and language, to improve the site content.</p>
    <p>Google Analytics uses first-party cookies to tell browsers and visit sessions apart. The active user count is a statistical estimate, and cross-device visits, browser restrictions and analytics blocking affect the results.</p>
    <p>In the page view records we configured, page addresses only contain the site and path, and sources only contain the source site. Ad personalization and Google Signals are turned off. The data is processed by Google; for details, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites?hl=en">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>.</p>
    <p>You can limit cookies in your browser's privacy settings, or use the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout/">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a> to limit analytics.</p>
    <section lang="en">
      <h2>Website analytics and privacy</h2>
      <p>This website and its documentation use Google Analytics 4 to measure active users, page views, referral sites, and basic device and language information. Google uses first-party cookies to distinguish browsers and sessions. User counts are estimates affected by multiple devices, browser restrictions, and blockers.</p>
      <p>Our page-view configuration sends the page origin and path, and the referring origin. Google Signals and advertising personalization are disabled. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites?hl=en">how Google uses information from partner sites</a>. You can restrict cookies in your browser or use the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout/">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
<style>
  .privacy-page { max-width: 820px; padding-block: 60px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(30px, 6vw, 42px); margin-block: 35px 25px; }
  h2 { font-size: 25px; margin-top: 40px; }
  p { line-height: 1.85; }
  p a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
